barrage array channel end (2026-11-28): Typhoeus's Barrage Array with the data's channel end (frame 215).

What it does: drops the kit's dataOverride `latest` on both combos' `area` hits, so the array's ticks get
KitHit.latestFrame 215 (the entity's 180 frames from its first tick at 35), as every other capped channel since round
22 (skillCompile.ts, a channel in a detached file): the placement joins no tick past it (logcasts.ts `pastChannel`) and
the replay lands none past it (drivers.ts replayCast).

Measured (`npm run measure -- --at HEAD --base HEAD --patch`, on 9da9d4a with the compiler's filter dropped and no
mark): verified |damage error| 1.4 → 1.5% (dbae −2.6 → −3.0%); development plain 84.3%, |damage error| 1.3 → 1.5% (00ae
1.1 → 3.9%, fc63 plain 527 → 530 but 3.2 → 5.9%, 1cd1 −2.2 → −2.3%); hold-out plain 82.5 → 82.4%, 5.9 → 6.0% (2 worse:
plain −6); 9c6e's totals moved.

Why dropped: the logs have the array's 18 ticks up to 6.4–8.0 s of world time after the first with no combo press
between (00ae 23.46, 54.96, 75.23, 94.24 s; fc63 35.98, 80.30 s): the end split each into two combos the log has no
press for, and the replay dropped the late ticks. What would make it work: the array's own clock (its entity held by
stops the placement's world time doesn't take out, or a life longer than 180 frames), read from these logs; its first
tick is logged 0.5–0.7 s after the press against the kit's frame 35 (1.17 s), a second sign its timing is off.

